{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Severstal Steel Defect Detection - Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project:** 10 - Severstal Steel Defect Detection  \n",
    "    "    "\n",
    "## Goals of this notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Load `train.csv` and inspect annotation schema (RLE format, per-image-per-class rows).\n",
    "2. Quantify class imbalance: per-class image counts and per-class pixel counts.\n",
    "3. Inspect a sample of images per class and overlay decoded masks.\n",
    "4. Distribution of mask area per defect class.\n",
    "5. Co-occurrence matrix: which classes appear together on the same image.\n",
    "6. Sanity checks: image dimensions, file integrity, missing files.\n",
    "\n",
    "All cells below are implementationed but NOT executed. Run end-to-end in main session after `kaggle competitions download -c severstal-steel-defect-detection` is unzipped into `../data/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports and paths"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path('../data')\n",
    "TRAIN_CSV = DATA_DIR / 'train.csv'\n",
    "TRAIN_IMG_DIR = DATA_DIR / 'train_images'\n",
    "TEST_IMG_DIR = DATA_DIR / 'test_images'\n",
    "IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH = 256, 1600\n",
    "NUM_CLASSES = 4\n",
    "\n",
    "print('train.csv exists:', TRAIN_CSV.exists())\n",
    "print('train_images dir exists:', TRAIN_IMG_DIR.exists())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load and reshape annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "`train.csv` has one row per `(image_id, class_id)` pair. Pivot to one row per image with four mask columns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv(TRAIN_CSV)\n",
    "print('Raw rows:', len(df))\n",
    "print(df.head())\n",
    "df.info()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[['ImageId', 'ClassId']] = df['ImageId_ClassId'].str.rsplit('_', n=1, expand=True)\n",
    "df['ClassId'] = df['ClassId'].astype(int)\n",
    "df['has_defect'] = df['EncodedPixels'].notna()\n",
    "wide = df.pivot_table(index='ImageId', columns='ClassId', values='has_defect', aggfunc='first', fill_value=False)\n",
    "wide.columns = [f'class_{c}' for c in wide.columns]\n",
    "wide['n_defects'] = wide.sum(axis=1)\n",
    "wide.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Schema and missingness"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Unique images:', df['ImageId'].nunique())\n",
    "print('Total annotation rows:', len(df))\n",
    "print('Rows with non-empty mask:', df['has_defect'].sum())\n",
    "print('Rows with empty mask:', (~df['has_defect']).sum())\n",
    "print('Image-level defect counts:')\n",
    "print(wide['n_defects'].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Class imbalance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "per_class_imgs = df[df['has_defect']].groupby('ClassId')['ImageId'].nunique().rename('images_with_defect')\n",
    "print(per_class_imgs)\n",
    "ax = per_class_imgs.plot.bar(color=['#38bdf8', '#a78bfa', '#f472b6', '#fbbf24'])\n",
    "ax.set_title('Images containing each defect class')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Defect class')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Number of images')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def rle_to_pixel_count(rle):\n",
    "    if not isinstance(rle, str) or rle.strip() == '':\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    parts = rle.split()\n",
    "    return sum(int(parts[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(parts), 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "df['pixels'] = df['EncodedPixels'].apply(rle_to_pixel_count)\n",
    "per_class_px = df.groupby('ClassId')['pixels'].sum()\n",
    "print('Pixel-area per defect class:')\n",
    "print(per_class_px)\n",
    "print('\\nFraction of total annotated defect pixels:')\n",
    "print((per_class_px / per_class_px.sum()).round(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Co-occurrence matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "Which classes tend to appear together on the same image? This matters because the four output channels are not mutually exclusive at training time, the network must support multi-label per pixel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "co = wide[['class_1', 'class_2', 'class_3', 'class_4']].astype(int)\n",
    "co_matrix = co.T @ co\n",
    "print(co_matrix)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 4))\n",
    "im = ax.imshow(co_matrix.values, cmap='magma')\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(4)); ax.set_yticks(range(4))\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels(['c1','c2','c3','c4']); ax.set_yticklabels(['c1','c2','c3','c4'])\n",
    "ax.set_title('Class co-occurrence (image counts)')\n",
    "for i in range(4):\n",
    "    for j in range(4):\n",
    "        ax.text(j, i, co_matrix.values[i, j], ha='center', va='center', color='white')\n",
    "plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Sample image and mask visualisation\n",
    "\n",
    "Decode a handful of RLE strings and overlay them on the underlying images, one per class. The Severstal RLE convention is column-major flattening, which differs from many other Kaggle conventions; the decoder below handles this correctly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def rle_decode(rle, shape=(IMG_HEIGHT, IMG_WIDTH)):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Severstal RLE decoder. Pixels are flattened column-major.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if not isinstance(rle, str) or rle.strip() == '':\n",
    "        return np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "    parts = rle.split()\n",
    "    starts = np.array(parts[0::2], dtype=int) - 1\n",
    "    lengths = np.array(parts[1::2], dtype=int)\n",
    "    flat = np.zeros(shape[0] * shape[1], dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "    for s, l in zip(starts, lengths):\n",
    "        flat[s:s + l] = 1\n",
    "    return flat.reshape(shape[1], shape[0]).T\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(NUM_CLASSES, 1, figsize=(14, 8))\n",
    "for cls in range(1, NUM_CLASSES + 1):\n",
    "    sample = df[(df['ClassId'] == cls) & df['has_defect']].iloc[0]\n",
    "    img = np.array(Image.open(TRAIN_IMG_DIR / sample['ImageId']).convert('L'))\n",
    "    mask = rle_decode(sample['EncodedPixels'])\n",
    "    axes[cls - 1].imshow(img, cmap='gray')\n",
    "    axes[cls - 1].imshow(np.ma.masked_where(mask == 0, mask), cmap='Reds', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "    axes[cls - 1].set_title(f'Class {cls} - {sample[\"ImageId\"]}')\n",
    "    axes[cls - 1].axis('off')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Mask area distribution per class\n",
    "\n",
    "Per-defect-instance pixel counts inform the loss-function choice: severe right-skew with many tiny masks is what motivates the focal Tversky loss in the advanced model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(11, 7), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n",
    "for cls, ax in zip(range(1, 5), axes.ravel()):\n",
    "    sub = df[(df['ClassId'] == cls) & df['has_defect']]['pixels']\n",
    "    ax.hist(np.log10(sub.clip(lower=1)), bins=40, color=f'C{cls-1}', alpha=0.8)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'Class {cls} - log10(mask pixels)')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('log10 mask area')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Count')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Image dimension and integrity check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "shapes = Counter()\n",
    "broken = []\n",
    "for f in list(TRAIN_IMG_DIR.glob('*.jpg'))[:500]:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        with Image.open(f) as im:\n",
    "            shapes[im.size] += 1\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        broken.append((f.name, str(e)))\n",
    "print('Image-shape distribution (sample of 500):', shapes)\n",
    "print('Broken files:', broken)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Background-pixel proportion\n",
    "\n",
    "A back-of-envelope estimate of the per-pixel class-imbalance ratio that the loss function has to overcome."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_imgs = wide.shape[0]\n",
    "total_px = n_imgs * IMG_HEIGHT * IMG_WIDTH\n",
    "defect_px = df[df['has_defect']]['pixels'].sum()\n",
    "print(f'Images: {n_imgs:,}')\n",
    "print(f'Total pixels: {total_px:,}')\n",
    "print(f'Defect pixels: {defect_px:,}  ({100 * defect_px / total_px:.2f}% of total)')\n",
    "print(f'Background:    {total_px - defect_px:,}  ({100 * (total_px - defect_px) / total_px:.2f}%)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. EDA takeaways (to feed into modelling)\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Multi-label task at the pixel level** - the four classes can co-occur, so the network needs four independent sigmoid heads, not a softmax.\n",
    "2. **Severe class imbalance** - background pixels dominate (~98-99%) and class 2 is roughly an order of magnitude rarer than class 3. Dice + BCE is a reasonable baseline; focal Tversky targets the rare classes more aggressively.\n",
    "3. **Long, thin defect geometry** - masks are typically elongated along the rolling direction. Horizontal flips and small horizontal shifts are reasonable augmentations; vertical flips are also safe because illumination is symmetric on a hot-rolled surface.\n",
    "4. **Image dimensions are uniform** at 256 x 1600. For SegFormer training, sliding-window or random 256 x 800 crops are the natural input size that keeps GPU memory usage manageable.\n",
    "5. **Validation strategy** - stratify the train/val split so each defect class appears at the same rate in train and val. A simple multilabel-aware random split with `iterstrat.MultilabelStratifiedKFold` is the standard choice."
   ]
  }
 ],
